This package contains material derived from KaTeX (https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX),
used under the MIT license reproduced below.

Two distinct kinds of derived material are present:

1. Source code — `src/kernel/` is KaTeX's parse and layout kernel, copied by
   `scripts/vendor-katex.ts` from upstream commit
   5a5bf2060431aaed5eb3b549f6fab24f55e9e70a with the MathML builders and the DOM
   emission methods removed. `src/registry/defineFunction.ts` and
   `src/registry/defineEnvironment.ts` are hand-written reductions of the
   upstream files of the same name. See `src/kernel/VENDORED.md`.

2. Font outline data — `src/glyphs/*.json` holds glyph contours and advance
   widths extracted from the KaTeX_* TrueType fonts by
   `scripts/generate-glyphs.ts`. KaTeX licenses its fonts under the same MIT
   terms as its code (`license: "MIT"` in both the repository and the published
   katex@0.16.11 package, whose LICENSE is byte-identical to the repository's),
   so this notice covers them too. The fonts themselves are derived from
   Computer Modern and the MathJax TeX fonts.

The SVG emit layer (`src/emit/`), the build scripts, and the tests are original
VectoJS work under the repository's own license. KaTeX has no SVG output target,
which is why that layer exists.

